![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

To adhere to the general rules, we should avoid using `Intl.Collator` with an undefined locale for sorting, as it can introduce locale-sensitive discrepancies across different runtime environments. Instead, we should define and use a strict lexicographical byte-order comparison helper to ensure locale-independent, deterministic ordering.

```javascript
const compareByteOrder = (left, right) => {
  const sLeft = String(left ?? '');
  const sRight = String(right ?? '');
  if (sLeft === sRight) return 0;
  return sLeft < sRight ? -1 : 1;
};

